WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:01.901
-Hey, everybody.

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.469
Welcome to "Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:05.604
It's me, Jimmy Fallon saying
hello and thank you so much

00:00:05.604 --> 00:00:07.474
for watching
on a Wednesday night.

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:10.443
The week is halfway over,
it's basically Thursday.

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:12.845
So, you know, good job,
everybody.

00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:14.447
Way to stay home.
Way to wear masks.

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:16.549
We're doing the right thing,
we're flattening that curve.

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:19.319
Come on, we got this, guys.
Let's go. It's Wednesday.

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.354
Two more days?
Come on, we got this, right?

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.656
Then the weekend's here.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:26.325
Yeah, which is basically what
today feels like.

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:27.793
Anyway, it doesn't matter.

00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:29.262
Let's start with some jokes.
How about this?

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.596
I'm very excited about this.

00:00:30.596 --> 00:00:32.031
My guest tonight is

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:34.300
New York Governor
Andrew Cuomo.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.335
Oh, my goodness.

00:00:36.335 --> 00:00:38.171
I called Governor Cuomo
yesterday and I said,

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:41.107
"Hey, man, you busy tomorrow?"
And he was like, "Not at all.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.143
No, not doing anything
right now.

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:44.910
I'm actually --
yeah, kind of bored.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.145
I need stuff to do.

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:47.914
Yeah, I definitely want to do
your show, Jimmy.

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:49.182
Thank you."

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:51.050
So that's cool, he's doing that.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.119
Guys, this Sunday
is Mother's Day.

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.421
Oh...
-[ Giggles ]

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:57.757
I saw that Louis Vuitton
released a series

00:00:57.757 --> 00:01:00.226
of free e-cards.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:02.094
What's better than watching
mom's face when she gets

00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:04.163
something from Louis Vuitton
and realizes

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:05.799
it's just an e-card?

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:13.172
Wow.

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:16.575
What?
[ Laughs ]

00:01:16.575 --> 00:01:18.578
My mom would go level.

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:22.215
My mom would cry.
She would cry, right?

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:25.117
She would go off and just start
secretly crying somewhere.

00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:27.153
-Mm-hmm.
Or nothing, really.

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:28.888
-[ Thick New York accent ]
"I just thought --

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:32.691
I opened up the card
and it's a Louis Vuitton.

00:01:32.691 --> 00:01:35.695
I thought you got me a new bag.

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:38.631
And it's just a card.
It's very thoughtful."

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:41.701
[ Laughs ]

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.836
I can't believe this.
There's a new TikTok trend

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:45.638
that's going viral --
oh, come on,

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:48.207
it's called the
Pee Your Pants Challenge.

00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:50.677
And it's basically
what it sounds like.

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:52.812
When I first saw it,
I thought, you know what?

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:54.914
We deserve the murder hornets.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:59.152
Listen to this, researchers
have found that otters

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:02.988
are more likely to juggle rocks
or pebbles when they're hungry.

00:02:02.988 --> 00:02:06.091
So if you're keeping track,
that's otter juggling study one,

00:02:06.091 --> 00:02:08.561
coronavirus vaccine, zero.

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:13.832
But the otter study,
with the juggled rocks

00:02:13.832 --> 00:02:16.536
when they're hungry,
yeah, that's proven.

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:19.738
So we got right on that one.

00:02:19.738 --> 00:02:21.373
A new study was published
showing evidence

00:02:21.373 --> 00:02:23.876
of ancient rivers on Mars.

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:25.711
Cool. Yeah, you could tell
they were rivers

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:28.247
because of all the ancient
Martian inner tubes

00:02:28.247 --> 00:02:30.750
and beer cans.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:34.820
A lot of tubing -- a little
Martian tubing up there.

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:39.391
[ Laughs ]

00:02:39.391 --> 00:02:41.728
Tubing.
Oh, man, that's great.

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:43.863
I read that the pandemic
could lead to the end

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:47.367
of crowded office meetings
with all of your co-workers.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:50.269
It's sad for the one guy who
loved hearing the really long

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:53.139
"Haaaaaa" at the beginning of
the happy birthday song.

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:55.674
♪ Haaaaaaappy... ♪

00:02:55.674 --> 00:02:58.211
Everyone. Aaaa...
Not yet.

00:02:58.211 --> 00:02:59.679
[ Sings ]

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.247
Don't start the harmony yet.

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:03.349
I know you're the one
who does the harmony.

00:03:06.118 --> 00:03:08.655
♪ To you ♪

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:12.191
My dog just left.

00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:13.960
Oh no, you're coming in.
Gary.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:16.929
You like that?
Did you think I called you?

00:03:16.929 --> 00:03:19.065
Man you're turning into kind of
a smelly dog.

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:20.766
I don't know what to do
with this dog.

00:03:20.766 --> 00:03:22.334
I really can't take it
right now.

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:23.869
Gary, you got
to get out of here.

00:03:23.869 --> 00:03:25.671
It's like being in like
a high school locker room.

00:03:25.671 --> 00:03:27.907
I'm not playing a game.
Oh no.

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:30.543
Whew! Gosh darn it.

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:32.645
Gary!

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:35.014
Man, that is something else,
man.

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:37.316
What is going down?

00:03:37.316 --> 00:03:39.919
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:42.054
-Gosh, Gary.

00:03:42.054 --> 00:03:44.857
I know you're a dog,
but are you, though?

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.792
We never knew you were a dog.

00:03:46.792 --> 00:03:48.060
[ Laughs ]

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:49.895
No, don't come --
I see the shadow.

00:03:49.895 --> 00:03:52.231
Gary.
No, we've had enough.

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:54.333
Now, you had the ball
and you were over there,

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:55.535
and everything was fine.

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:57.136
You were taking a nap,
remember that?

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:59.038
Go back to do that.

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:00.606
All right, go.
You can go out that way.

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:02.908
Good girl, good girl.
Go out that way.

00:04:02.908 --> 00:04:05.544
Lay down.
Lay down.

00:04:05.544 --> 00:04:08.181
Lay down. Lay down.

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:12.518
Whew!

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:17.623
It's like she rolled
in something insane, dude.

00:04:17.623 --> 00:04:19.558
What is happening?

00:04:19.558 --> 00:04:21.861
I can't even look at you.

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:23.528
It's not your fault,
it's all right.

00:04:23.528 --> 00:04:24.864
I'll take care of you.

00:04:29.202 --> 00:04:31.303
Sorry, Gary.

00:04:31.303 --> 00:04:35.374
I think I insulted her.
I'll give her a treat later.

00:04:35.374 --> 00:04:37.276
Is it the treats
we're giving her?

00:04:37.276 --> 00:04:38.978
-I do not know.
-I got her new treats.

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:41.247
-I don't know if she found
a nest and rolled in something

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:44.717
but the insane scrubbing
I gave her did not work, so.

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:48.654
-What in the what?
That is insanity.

00:04:48.654 --> 00:04:50.556
-...after this.

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:52.758
-This is interesting,
I heard about a company

00:04:52.758 --> 00:04:56.228
in South Africa that's offering
virtual safaris.

00:04:56.228 --> 00:04:58.631
Yeah, there's actually a name
for virtual safaris.

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:02.035
It's called
"watching National Geographic."

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:03.769
So...

00:05:03.769 --> 00:05:07.706
Kids, we got some
virtual safari now.

00:05:07.706 --> 00:05:10.743
I saw that Texas will soon
allow hair salons,

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:13.713
tanning salons,
and gyms to reopen.

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:16.549
Which explains why the state is
changing its name from Texas

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:18.351
to Newer Jersey.

00:05:18.351 --> 00:05:21.554
And finally, we've been seeing
a lot of great reporters --

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:24.524
TV reporters out there giving us
the news, and they're awesome.

00:05:24.524 --> 00:05:26.792
So thank you for doing all that
hard stuff, and that hard work.

00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:28.461
We really appreciate it.

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:30.463
But what we also realized
is that some of the interviews,

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:32.765
the lighter interviews,
people are wearing face masks,

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:35.001
and there's a way to make them
kind of say

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:36.269
whatever we want them to say

00:05:36.269 --> 00:05:37.836
because their face
is covered up.

00:05:37.836 --> 00:05:39.371
I don't know, we gave it
a shot.

00:05:39.371 --> 00:05:41.908
Check out this new bit
called "Face Mask the Nation."

00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:46.345
-♪ Face Mask the Nation ♪

00:05:46.345 --> 00:05:50.015 line:0%
-What is the short term plan
in Miami-Dade county

00:05:50.015 --> 00:05:51.584 line:0%
if they're not going to
necessarily be

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:53.552 line:0%
opening up the
beaches right now?

00:05:53.552 --> 00:05:58.390
-So the plan is to go into the
ocean and pull the drain plug,

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:02.528
drain out the ocean, and refill
it when it is safe to do so.

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:04.463 line:0%
-Let me show you how to
properly wear a mask.

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:05.931 line:0%
First you're going to want
to tug on it

00:06:05.931 --> 00:06:07.900 line:0%
with your filthy hands,
and then expose

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.268 line:0%
just a little bit of chin.

00:06:09.268 --> 00:06:11.504 line:0%
Tempt the virus.
Show a little skin.

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:13.973 line:0%
Flirt with her.
Hey, virus, how you doing?

00:06:13.973 --> 00:06:16.141 line:0%
-I just feel like you say
you want a commitment,

00:06:16.141 --> 00:06:18.678 line:0%
but then when I get closer,
you pull further away.

00:06:18.678 --> 00:06:20.613 line:0%
-Can I say something?
-And then when I back off,

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:22.348 line:0%
you tell me we feel distant.
-Are you done?

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:23.715 line:0%
-So I don't know what to do,
Amanda.

00:06:23.715 --> 00:06:25.617 line:0%
Because everything I do seems
to be the wrong thing.

00:06:25.617 --> 00:06:27.286 line:0%
-Rick, I know about Debra.

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:29.422
-Ha ha! That was our monologue,
everybody.

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:31.423
We have a great show tonight.
As I said earlier,

00:06:31.423 --> 00:06:34.727
Governor Andrew Cuomo
is on the show tonight.

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:37.262
Man, is he doing
an unbelievable job.

00:06:37.262 --> 00:06:38.897
Thank you so much,
Governor Cuomo.

00:06:38.897 --> 00:06:41.700
I got to talk to him about
everything that's going on

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:43.269
and what he's thinking
about everything

00:06:43.269 --> 00:06:44.737
and what the next steps are

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:48.741
and how great New York has been
handling all of this.

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:50.609
He's just a smart, smart guy

00:06:50.609 --> 00:06:52.378
and just really delivers
the facts.

00:06:52.378 --> 00:06:53.846
So, thank you for coming on.

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:56.415
We also have Gabrielle Union
on the show.

00:06:56.415 --> 00:06:58.684
Gabrielle is going to tell us
everything she's doing

00:06:58.684 --> 00:07:01.186
for the LGBTQ community
as well as team up

00:07:01.186 --> 00:07:03.155
with Questlove in a game
that we're going to play

00:07:03.155 --> 00:07:04.556
later on in the show.

00:07:04.556 --> 00:07:06.158
It's going to be fun.

00:07:06.158 --> 00:07:08.460
And also, we have great music
from Brad Paisley.

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:09.829
We love Brad Paisley.

00:07:09.829 --> 00:07:12.364
The song is called
"There's No I in Beer."

00:07:12.364 --> 00:07:14.900
[ Laughs ]

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:16.702
That is great, man.

00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:20.639
Oh, I thought of a country song.

00:07:20.639 --> 00:07:24.043
"When it Rains, I Pour."

00:07:24.043 --> 00:07:25.878
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:25.878 --> 00:07:27.379
-It's about a dude, right?

00:07:27.379 --> 00:07:29.148
When he's bummed out,
he goes to the booze.

00:07:29.148 --> 00:07:30.449
-I love it.
-It's not bad, right?

00:07:30.449 --> 00:07:32.685
-Love it.

00:07:32.685 --> 00:07:35.521
-Is it a song?
-Yeah. Is he depressed?

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:37.322
-No, I mean,
is it a song already?

00:07:37.322 --> 00:07:39.558
-Oh, no.
-All right, well...

00:07:39.558 --> 00:07:41.627
Hey, guys, it's Wednesday,
so we're going to do

00:07:41.627 --> 00:07:43.529
our bit called
"What Are You Doing Wednesdays."

00:07:43.529 --> 00:07:44.730
Here we go.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:47.166
-♪ What are you doing
this Wednesday? ♪

00:07:47.166 --> 00:07:49.835
♪ What are you
doing this Wednesday ♪

00:07:49.835 --> 00:07:51.504
-Hey, guys, we're doing
this thing on Wednesdays

00:07:51.504 --> 00:07:53.338
which I think I'm just going to
keep up with the show

00:07:53.338 --> 00:07:54.607
because it makes me laugh.

00:07:54.607 --> 00:07:56.308
It's "What Are You Doing
Wednesdays."

00:07:56.308 --> 00:07:58.143
I just see things,
people send me videos

00:07:58.143 --> 00:08:01.146
of people online doing something
that just makes me laugh.

00:08:01.146 --> 00:08:03.849
And so if it makes me laugh,
hopefully it will make you laugh

00:08:03.849 --> 00:08:05.351
and bring a smile on your face.

00:08:05.351 --> 00:08:07.352
The first one is from
Stefani Davis,

00:08:07.352 --> 00:08:10.288
who thought of a way to
play wine pong.

00:08:10.288 --> 00:08:13.025
Which, by the way, I think
I've heard of that before?

00:08:13.025 --> 00:08:17.730
I know beer pong.
Wine pong is a thing?

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:21.567
But she thought of a way to play
wine pong by herself.

00:08:21.567 --> 00:08:24.136 line:0%
Look at this thing.

00:08:24.136 --> 00:08:26.171 line:0%
-Mommy! [ Shouts ]

00:08:26.171 --> 00:08:28.908 line:0%
[ Excited chatter ]

00:08:28.908 --> 00:08:31.677 line:0%
-Oh, that's...
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:31.677 --> 00:08:32.678 line:0%
-Ha!

00:08:32.678 --> 00:08:34.013
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:37.116
"Hey, Mom?
Mom, can we come in?"

00:08:37.116 --> 00:08:41.887
"Uh, Mom's showering.
don't come in."

00:08:41.887 --> 00:08:44.290
This next one is called
"The Fence Hack."

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.158
And this is two
next-door neighbors,

00:08:46.158 --> 00:08:48.060
they find a way to make
their fence

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:49.628
work better
in their favor.

00:08:49.628 --> 00:08:50.629
Check it out.

00:08:50.629 --> 00:08:59.038
♪♪

00:08:59.038 --> 00:09:08.380
♪♪

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:11.817
♪♪

00:09:11.817 --> 00:09:13.919
-I mean, if that just doesn't
say America for you.

00:09:13.919 --> 00:09:16.088
And ingenuity and creativity
and awesome

00:09:16.088 --> 00:09:18.857
and friendly neighbors
and the kids and everyone.

00:09:18.857 --> 00:09:21.960
But distancing and just --

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:24.297
That is awesome, I love that.

00:09:24.297 --> 00:09:26.065
Thanks for doing that, guys.

00:09:26.065 --> 00:09:29.501
This last one here is from
@Alexpresley's family.

00:09:29.501 --> 00:09:31.370
They got bored.
They invented a new game.

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:33.538
And I think this game
is going to take off.

00:09:33.538 --> 00:09:36.041
I mean, bigger than football,
bigger than wrestling.

00:09:36.041 --> 00:09:39.779
This is the new thing, this is
family backslide race,

00:09:39.779 --> 00:09:41.781
where they're sliding
on their backs

00:09:41.781 --> 00:09:44.349
and racing around
into the living room.

00:09:44.349 --> 00:09:46.752
[ Laughs ] Watch this.

00:09:46.752 --> 00:09:49.055 line:0%
-On your mark, get set, go.

00:09:49.055 --> 00:09:50.723 line:0%
-Go, go, go.

00:09:50.723 --> 00:09:51.857 line:0%
-Oh!
-Wow.

00:09:51.857 --> 00:09:53.992 line:0%
-Oh, [indistinct]

00:09:53.992 --> 00:09:55.627 line:0%
So good!
-Oh!

00:09:55.627 --> 00:09:57.496 line:0%
-5:56.
-Whoo!

00:09:57.496 --> 00:09:59.098 line:0%
-Go!
-Go, Rudy, go, go.

00:09:59.098 --> 00:10:01.534 line:0%
-It's the mom.
[ Laughing ]

00:10:01.534 --> 00:10:04.403 line:0%
-She's moving.
[ Shouting ]

00:10:04.403 --> 00:10:06.605 line:0%
-[ Laughing ]
-Go!

00:10:06.605 --> 00:10:09.141 line:0%
-7:40.
-Not bad.

00:10:09.141 --> 00:10:12.278 line:0%
-Go.
[ Shouting ]

00:10:12.278 --> 00:10:15.147 line:0%
-Go, go, go, go, go!
-Whoo!

00:10:15.147 --> 00:10:16.381 line:0%
-Wow!

00:10:16.381 --> 00:10:17.883 line:0%
-[ Shouting ]

00:10:17.883 --> 00:10:19.351 line:0%
-4.2.

00:10:19.351 --> 00:10:22.021 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:10:22.021 --> 00:10:24.290
You see mom cooking
right there?

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:26.458
She was going for it.
I loved it so much.

00:10:26.458 --> 00:10:28.460
Guys, that was "What Are You
Doing Wednesdays."

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:29.695
Thank you so much.

